{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"My dear Marie,\n\nI am now sitting in The Hague and writing to you briefly about how today was in Antwerp. We crossed the Scheldt and arrived in the city, which, like Ghent, has a population of sixty to seventy thousand souls.\n\nI found the cathedral particularly strange. The nave has three rows of columns on each side, but there are neither benches nor pews. Instead, there are stacks of a hundred chairs there. Every visitor must now take a chair for himself and carry it from altar to altar. One can imagine the crowd dragging things back and forth to follow the service. It is a sight one does not forget so quickly, and it makes the spaciousness of the church lively in a very peculiar, almost restless way.\n\nThe evenings are cool here, but the company is friendly. I hope Karl and Immanuel are keeping up their end.\n\nYour faithful\nGeorg Wilhelm"}}],"created":1795221126,"model":"qwen","system_fingerprint":"b11429-d81235049","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":187,"prompt_tokens":292,"total_tokens":479,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-FITBabVv7XT0FEQQcpg4AWtft5205yZN","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":292,"prompt_ms":398.527,"prompt_per_token_ms":1.3648184931506848,"prompt_per_second":732.6981609778007,"predicted_n":187,"predicted_ms":4326.185,"predicted_per_token_ms":23.25905913978495,"predicted_per_second":42.99400048772764}}